    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0341" n="169" xml:id="pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/389</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Liverpool</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 10.80 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Harold E. Burke, American citizen, residing 24 Holmes
                    Court, Portsmouth, N. H., affirms member crew British schooner. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Mayola</hi>, St. John’s, Newfoundland-Alicante, Spain,
                    cargo fish, unarmed. German submarine commander, 4.15 p.m., February 16, ordered
                    abandon vessel, placed boinbs on board <hi rendition="#italic">Mayola</hi>. Crew
                    in palm sea, wind moderate, rowed 21 miles to Albufeira, Portugal. No other
                    Americans on board affidavit mailed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
